\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs34 ReaBackground\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Shows a muted video (synced to the play and edit cursor) or a still image behind REAPER's arrange view on macOS. Items, grid, cursors and overlays stay on top; the time selection, mute shading and grid lines read as shading over the video.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 After installing, restart REAPER, then run the action {\b ReaBackground.lua} (or Extensions > ReaBackground...) to open the settings window. Import a video or image with the + tile, click a thumbnail to use it in the current project, or the globe icon to make it the default for every project.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requirements: macOS 11 or newer, REAPER with Metal rendering enabled, ReaImGui (install it from ReaPack) for the settings window.\par}
}
